xperiments/window_sensitivity.txt","locator":"margins 12.12/17.88 mV; RL=320k -> 0.6239 V; leakage threshold 1.21 uA; Cs=2 nF -> dV=12.4 mV; dV/dt=0.368 mV/us; time window 0.9676-1.0498 ms"},{"path":"inputs/requirements.txt","locator":"lines 1-2: ADC parameters 'have not been specified'; 'do not invent ADC behavior'"},{"path":"work/netlist/design.xml","locator":"net /OUT: C1.1, J1.2, R1.2"}],"reasoning":"This is the central scope question. The design passes the criterion nominally and unloaded, but the stated operating condition (connected switched ADC) is unparameterized, and the quantified margins show that plausible magnitudes of ADC loading or sample-timing variation would decide pass/fail. Per the scope's own instruction this is missing coverage rather than an established defect, so it is reported as a major concern, not a defect."},{"id":"CIR-2","title":"No component tolerances stated; criterion window allows only -4.75%/+3.35% RC deviation","location":"inputs/project/rc_filter.kicad_sch (R1 Value '10k', C1 Value '100n'; no tolerance fields)","condition":"Meeting 0.62-0.65 V at exactly 1 ms requires the RC product to lie in [0.9525, 1.0335] ms, i.e. within -4.75%/+3.35% of the nominal 1.000 ms. The schematic specifies only nominal values with no tolerance, dielectric or part-number data.","mechanism":"V(1 ms) = 1 - exp(-1 ms/RC). Solving the window bounds gives the allowed RC range. Common 100 nF ceramic capacitors carry +/-10% (sometimes +/-5%) tolerance before temperature and DC-bias effects, which alone exceeds the +3.35% / -4.75% budget; a +/-1% resistor adds further spread. With no tolerance specification in the candidate, compliance is guaranteed only for exactly-nominal parts.","severity":"minor","assessment":"concern","evidence":[{"path":"review-work/circuit/experiments/window_sensitivity.txt","locator":"RC product must lie in [0.9525, 1.0335] ms => -4.75% .. +3.35% allowed deviation"},{"path":"inputs/project/rc_filter.kicad_sch","locator":"C1 property Value \"100n\" (symbol uuid 1dcaf7b4...), R1 property Value \"10k\" (symbol uuid c5c38e1a...); no tolerance properties present"}],"reasoning":"No tolerance requirement is stated, so I do not assert a violation; but the window implied by the stated criterion is tighter than typical off-the-shelf capacitor tolerance, and the candidate contains no data showing the parts selected can hold it. Flagged as a minor concern / coverage gap rather than a defect, consistent with 'do not impose unstated ratings'."},{"id":"CIR-3","title":"Output transits the window rather than settling; 'settles at 1 ms' is only an instantaneous sample","location":"inputs/requirements.txt line 1; /OUT step response","condition":"The unloaded step response does not settle in the 0.62-0.65 V band: it passes through it near t=1 ms and continues to 0.8647 V at 2 ms and 1.0 V asymptotically. The criterion is satisfiable only as an instantaneous measurement at t=1 ms.","mechanism":"First-order RC with tau=1 ms rises monotonically toward the 1 V input; the band 0.62-0.65 V is occupied only during t in [0.9676, 1.0498] ms. Any reading of 'settles' as a steady-state requirement is unmeetable by this topology; any reading as a sampled value makes the result sensitive to the (unspecified) sampling instant at 0.368 mV/us.","severity":"info","assessment":"concern","evidence":[{"path":"review-work/circuit/experiments/rc_step.cir","locator":"vout_at_1ms=0.6321 V, vout_at_2ms=0.8647 V"},{"path":"review-work/circuit/experiments/window_sensitivity.txt","locator":"in-band time interval 0.9676-1.0498 ms; slope 0.368 mV/us at 1 ms"}],"reasoning":"Interpretation note for the adjudicator: under the instantaneous-sample reading the nominal design passes (CIR-1 evidence); under a steady-state reading no simple RC from a 1 V step can comply. Recorded at info level because the requirement wording, not the candidate hardware, is the source of ambiguity, and sampling timing is explicitly listed as unspecified."}]},"caller":